-- title:
--   Exhaustion of corep(O^{nr})×Ω by Noetherian subalgebras
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime, let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative domain of characteristic $0$ which is a discrete valuation ring, let $\pi \in \mathcal O$ be irreducible, assume $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, that $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements and that the ideal generated by the image of $r$ is $(\pi)$; let $K_0$ be a field of characteristic $0$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra and a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be a commutative domain of characteristic $0$ and $\mathcal O$-algebra such that $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo it, and every monic polynomial of positive degree over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ has a root modulo it. Let $B$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent. Write $F$ for the functor on commutative $\mathcal O$-algebras sending $C$ to the pairs $(\psi, d)$ with $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to_{\mathcal O} C$ an algebra map and $d$ a Deligne datum over $C$ (a family of $C$-submodules $d(M) \subseteq C \otimes_{\mathcal O} M$, one for each full $\mathcal O$-lattice $M$ in $K_0^2$, with invertible quotients, compatible with lattice inclusions and with the homothety action, and satisfying the $\pi$-nondegeneracy condition at every prime of $C$), and acting on algebra maps $f$ by $\psi \mapsto f \circ \psi$ and by base change of the lines along $f$. The assertion is the conjunction of three statements. First, every $x = (\psi, d) \in F(B)$ lies in the image of $F(S) \to F(B)$ induced by the inclusion of $S$, for some finite $s \subseteq B$ and $S = \mathcal O[\,\mathrm{range}\,\psi \cup s\,] \subseteq B$. Second, given $x \in F(B)$, finite sets $s_1, s_2 \subseteq B$, the subalgebras $S_i = \mathcal O[\,\mathrm{range}\,\psi \cup s_i\,]$ and elements $x_i \in F(S_i)$ both mapping to $x$, there are a finite $s_3 \subseteq B$ and $S_3 = \mathcal O[\,\mathrm{range}\,\psi \cup s_3\,]$ with $S_1 \le S_3$, $S_2 \le S_3$ and with the images of $x_1$ and $x_2$ in $F(S_3)$ equal. Third, for every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ and every finite $s \subseteq B$, the subalgebra $\mathcal O[\,\mathrm{range}\,\psi \cup s\,]$ is a Noetherian ring.
--
--   Together the three clauses say that $F(B) = \varinjlim_s F(\mathcal O[\psi(O^{\mathrm{nr}}) \cup s])$ over the directed system of subalgebras generated by the image of the fixed coefficient map and finitely many further elements, each of which is Noetherian; here $B$ is only assumed $\pi$-nilpotent. It is the local-finiteness input used by the extension, gluing and lifting results for the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison functor, which are proved first over Noetherian test algebras and then transported to arbitrary $\pi$-nilpotent ones.
